From cba4995ea4c21673afc3b873779f1d6a5fa03e69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:25:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Complete the response for the turn that ended

isCompleteObs lives on the chat session, so both turn-end paths complete
whichever response is current rather than the one belonging to the turn that
ended. When two turns overlap, the outgoing turn closes the incoming turn's
response and every later progress batch is dropped into it, leaving the turn
rendered empty with no stop button.

Measured against a dev container: with a text-only turn the preempted turn
ends ~500ms before the next turn's request is created and everything renders,
but a turn ending tool calls trails it by ~5ms and sixteen progress batches
were discarded.

The response now records the turn that claims it, and an end signal from any
other turn is ignored. A response nothing has claimed is still completed by
whichever turn ends, so sequential turns are unchanged.

The rule is extracted as a predicate so it can be tested without standing up
a chat session, as unwrapSessionLoadErrorMessage in the same file is.
---
